> >In particular, while opinions overall vary wildly, I think it's almost
> >universally agreed that lingering on an explored level purely to increase
> >XL is a bad plan in the early game.
> 
> Actually David is there any good time in a game for hanging around an
> explored level to purely increase XL?

When i learned to play NetHack, i did develop the habit of not going
to a dungeonlevel when i hadn't achieved the same XP yet, so ended up
hanging around on Dlvl One for a bit if the starting population wasn't
enough for the first level-up. The necessarily rising monster
difficulty notwithstanding, added hitpoints and better chance to hit
stuff were a notable benefit. 

Of course, i didn't know about the weird way NetHack has of counting
in your xp when generating fresh monsters. I still think keeping XP
equal to DL is a good general tactic until about Dlvl8 for combat
wombats. Less good for the notoriously poor hand-to-hand fighters -
archeologist, healer and tourist; those are desperately in need of
upgrading their combat gear, and doing so whilst facing weaker foes
(i.e. while advancing XP at a slower pace, not while sticking to XP:1)
is a very good idea indeed.

